          <strong>💡 Explanation:</strong> Although there's a Three-Way Rule baseline that gives all ATM customers 40 firewall rules, CORD company has a Four-Way Rule exception that overrides it with 50 custom rules. Four-Way Rules are checked at Level 2 (higher priority than Three-Way Rules at Level 4), so CORD gets their custom configuration while all other ATM customers get the standard 40 rules.
